 { On this occasion, the defender's task is even more difficult, being two pawns down and about to lose a third one. However, Keres spots a strong plan in practice: attack the f3-pawn with both pieces in order to create a passed pawn. } 1. { -KEY- } Qb6+ Kg5 $1 2. Qxa5 Qe2 ( { Of course not } 2... Kf4 $2 3. Qe5 ) 
3. Qc3 f4 4. Ka2 { Now that 4...Qd1+ can no longer be met by 5.Qc1 check, Taimanov parries this threat in advance. } Kh4 5. d5 Kg3 { Black has improved his pieces to a maximum, and further actions now depends on White's play. } 6. Ka3 $6 ( { So far White has played well, but here he misses an easier win: } 6. Qd4 $1 Kxf3 7. d6 { - Taimanov. At the cost of just one pawn White has centralized his queen, which now limits the enemy checks and provides the passed d-pawn with excellent support. } ) 
Qd1 { Obviously, the f3-pawn cannot be taken. } 7. Qb3 Qd2 8. Ka2 $6 ( 8. Qc4 $1 { was stronger, with the idea } Kxf3 9. Qc3 { - Taimanov. After } Qxc3 10. bxc3 Ke2 11. d6 f3 12. d7 f2 13. d8=Q $11 f1=Q $11 14. Qd5 $1 { (centralization first), Black is unlikely to save himself. } ) 
Qd4 $1 { Centralizing the queen and tying White to the defence of his pawns. } 9. Kb1 $6 ( { Taimanov might have discarded } 9. a5 { in view of } Qc5 { and Black wins a pawn back, although after } 10. Qc3 Qxd5 11. Ka3 { White keeps excellent winning chances. } ) 
Qg1+ 10. Kc2 Qc5+ 11. Kd2 Qd4+ 12. Ke2 ( { The last chance for a win was probably } 12. Kc2 { followed by Kb1-a2, reverting to the previous note. } ) 
Kg2 $1 ( { Seeing that } 12... Qf2 13. Kd3 Qxf3 14. Kc4 { leads to a bad ending after } Qxb3 15. Kxb3 f3 16. d6 f2 17. d7 f1=Q $11 18. d8=Q $11 Qf7 19. Ka3 { Keres avoids the pin along the third rank in advance, while awaiting the opponent's next step. } ) 
13. a5 Qf2+ 14. Kd1 ( { Or } 14. Kd3 Qxf3 15. Kc4 Qe4 $1 { (compare the previous note) } 16. Kc5 f3 { and Black won't lose. } ) 
Qd4+ 15. Kc1 Qe3+ $1 16. Kc2 Qc5+ $2 { A strange error - or perhaps a misprint. } ( { a) } 16... Qe2 { maintained the perpetual, since } 17. Kb1 Qe1 18. Ka2 { fails to } Qxa5 ) 
 ( { b) Instead, after } 16... Qc5 { a draw was agreed, though here } 17. Qc3 $1 Qxd5 18. Qd2 { led to a win - Taimanov. Beyond the turbulent conclusion of the battle, Black's defence was truly heroic in this game. } ) 

 1/2-1/2

